# The proxy every Yandex host is fetched through: a URL-prefix proxy inside CIS,
# the whole destination URL appended to it.
#
# Committed, because it's public the moment the bundle ships and a clone should
# build something that works. It has to be **https**, or the deployed page can't
# fetch it — mixed content. Override it in `.env.local` (gitignored) or with a
# real `VITE_YM_PROXY` in the environment, which wins over any .env file.
#
# It's inlined at build time, so a new address means a rebuild, not just an edit.
# This file on **master** is also what a deployed client re-reads when its own
# built-in address stops answering, so keep the line machine-readable:
# `VITE_YM_PROXY=<https url>`, which is what `update-proxy.yml` writes.
#
# Leaving it unset talks to Yandex directly, and that is **not** enough even
# inside CIS: api.music.yandex.net sends no CORS headers to this app's origin,
# so the browser blocks it wherever you are. Being in CIS drops the geoblock,
# not the CORS half — see "The proxy" in CLAUDE.md.
VITE_YM_PROXY=https://voters-outer-applications-machine.trycloudflare.com/
